Hi Christine,

I wanted to share one dispatch example concerning a stop condition. In the in=
terview, the participant opened the stop row and its Note. They described an =
earlier handoff in which they compared the Note with a paper exception memo, =
found an additional condition on the paper, and passed that condition verball=
y to the next dispatcher.

I've attached a short note with the participant's anonymized words and the li=
mits of what we can say from this account. We observed the opening of the sto=
p row in the interview; the comparison and verbal handoff were described by t=
he participant. The participant did not see how the next person handled the c=
ondition afterward, so we cannot report the outcome. This is one example, not=
 a conclusion about general screen requirements or other participants.

Best,
Jennifer

